-- title:
--   Surjectivity criterion for maps out of adically complete rings
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ and $R$ be commutative rings (in a common universe), let $J \subseteq P$ be an ideal such that $P$ is $J$-adically complete (separated and precomplete for the $J$-adic filtration), and let $I \subseteq R$ be an ideal such that $R$ is $I$-adically Hausdorff, i.e. an element of $R$ lying in every $I^{n}$ is zero. Let $\varphi : P \to R$ be a ring homomorphism subject to three conditions: the ideal of $R$ generated by $\varphi(J)$ is contained in $I$; $\varphi$ is surjective modulo $I$, in the sense that for every $r \in R$ there is $p \in P$ with $r - \varphi(p) \in I$; and $I \le \varphi(J)R + I^{2}$, where $\varphi(J)R$ denotes the ideal generated by the image of $J$. The conclusion is that $\varphi$ is surjective as a map of underlying sets. Note that completeness is required only of the source and mere separatedness only of the target; in particular $R$ is not assumed complete.
--
--   This is the standard criterion (as in Matsumura, Commutative Ring Theory, Theorem 8.4) that a homomorphism from an adically complete ring which is surjective modulo the ideal and surjective on the first graded piece, i.e. on relative cotangent data, is surjective. It is used in the identification of suitable complete local rings with rings of formal power series, via [`IsLocalRing.exists_powerSeries_algEquiv_apply_X_eq_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_ringKrullDim_eq_two`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_powerSeries_algEquiv_apply_X_eq_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_ringKrullDim_eq_two).
